course: dictionary
lesson: 12376
title: Crumpets and tea-time words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a food you may not have eaten yet, but you can still work out what they mean from the words around them. «On cold afternoons, Mum toasted a crumpet by the fire and spread butter on it.» Toasted, butter and cold afternoons are clues. A crumpet is something you toast and eat hot.
explain: Describing words are clues too. «The crumpets were round and flat, with small holes all over the top.» Round, flat and holes tell you what a crumpet looks like, even if you have never seen one.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try «On cold afternoons, Mum toasted a round, flat bread cake by the fire.» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: A crumpet is a round, flat, soft bread cake with small holes on top.
fact: Crumpets are usually toasted and eaten hot, with butter.
fact: Crumpets with butter and jam or honey are a classic tea-time treat in Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the animals enjoy hot buttered toast and cosy teas by the fire, the kind of food crumpets belong to.
fact: In Canada and the US, a similar food is called an English muffin.
exercise: «Sam spread honey on his warm crumpet at tea-time.» Which word tells you a crumpet is eaten hot? | Honey | *Warm | Spread | Tea-time
exercise: «On cold afternoons, Mum toasted a crumpet by the fire.» What is a crumpet? | A tea-time game | A cold drink | *A round, flat bread cake, eaten hot | A small pet that lives by the fire
exercise: In Canada and the US, what is a similar food called? | Cornflake | Crisp | *English muffin | Pizza
test: «Dad toasted two crumpets and spread them with butter and jam.» What did Dad do to the crumpets? | Dropped them in the sea | Froze them | *Toasted them | Painted them
test: Which picture words describe a crumpet? | Square and made of metal | *Round and flat with small holes on top | Blue and round like a ball | Long and thin like a stick
exam: What does crumpet mean in «Lily ate a hot crumpet with honey at tea-time»? | A cold drink | A tea-time game | A small pet | *A round, flat bread cake
